{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For there was no house where there was no one dead</b> — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 12:30): if there was a firstborn there — dead; if there was no firstborn there — the eldest of the house was dead, for he is called \"בכור\" (firstborn), as it is stated (Psalms 89:27), \"I also shall make him the בכור.\" Another interpretation: the Egyptian women were promiscuous under their husbands and bore children from bachelors, and they had many firstborns — sometimes five to one woman, each one a firstborn to his father. But according to the plain sense, the firstborns who died in Egypt were בכורי פטר רחם (firstborns that open the womb), and therefore He consecrated under them every firstborn that opens the womb among the children of Israel, both man and beast (Exodus 13:2), and the firstborn of Pharaoh sitting on his throne (Exodus 12:29) was פטר רחם (the first to open the womb) of his mother, and so is the custom of kings that the reigning queen is a virgin, as is stated regarding Ahasuerus (Esther 2:3). But according to the opinion of our Sages, the resolution is that He smote in Egypt \"כל בכוריהם\" (all their firstborns), meaning the firstborn of the father — ראשית אונו (the first of his vigor) — and the firstborn of the mother — פטר רחם (the one that opens the womb) — and also the eldest of the house; but He did not wish to consecrate under them among Israel except the firstborn of the mother, for that is more well-known and publicized, and in the case of beasts it is not known at all except the firstborn of the mother, and He selected that species from among all of them. And a similar proof for this: \"And He smote every firstborn in Egypt, ראשית אונים (the first of vigor) in the tents of Ham\" (Psalms 78:51) — for this expression is used of the male."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "Rashi's second interpretation begins with ד\"א (דבר אחר, 'another interpretation'); I have rendered it as such."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:06:49.411735003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}